60,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Option A sounds like a game, but I hate the plugging-in part! I vote for C!","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option A is the most efficient for area billing, but Option C avoids the cost of constant re-wiring.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,Option A is unfair to those who arrive late; they'll always get the worst seats. I prefer B.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option A is a nightmare. Constant noise and zero ergonomic stability. Option C is the only logical choice.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Yumi,,Option A means I get to sit next to someone different every day! But the cost... maybe B is a good middle ground?,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Mizuki, if we do B, do we have to move all our stuff? That sounds like those messy shuffles!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"Option B still incurs the ""shuffling"" cost and doesn't solve the billing issue as well as A.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, it's better than some people being stuck in the dark for a whole year while others have the window.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"The ""dark"" is a minor inconvenience compared to the physical strain of a poorly fitted chair. C is the only way to maintain a setup.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Yumi,,I love the idea of B because we get to rotate who we're close to! It keeps the energy fresh!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'm sticking with C. I want to come in and just start working!,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"Given the budget constraints and the cost of power re-runs, C is the most fiscally responsible.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"If we go with C, we must explicitly agree on how the ""bad"" seats are assigned. I can't support it otherwise.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,We can assign the quietest seats to those with the highest focus requirements. That is a logical distribution.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"If we do C, I'll just have to make a huge effort to walk over and talk to everyone! I can do that!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Rin,,Yay! Let's just decide!,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I've made my decision.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I will concede to C, provided we are honest about the seat quality.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shion,,Finally. A decision based on stability.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I'm happy as long as we're all happy! Let's vote!,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
